AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.md
z_history/
**/z_history/
**/scenario.json.bak
**/_scratch/
**/.pytest_cache/
tests/node_modules/
tests/test-results/
tests/playwright-report/
.DS_Store
# cinemagraph raw pre-loop clips — kept locally so a loop can be switched (boomerang↔crossfade) without
# re-generating; the player never needs them, so don't push them to the public site.
**/*_raw.mp4
**/*.reloop.mp4
# pre-edit cinemagraph originals (the picked/played clip keeps the plain name)
**/*_orig.mp4

# --- Keep the public repo to PLAY-REQUIRED assets only (2026-08-06) ---
# Rule: only files the player fetches at runtime (scenario.json, play.html, referenced
# panoramas/cinemagraphs/audio/images, data CSVs, shared engine, decoder) belong on the
# public site. Authoring records, build caches, backups, and history-tier dirs do not.
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT untrack already-committed files — after this syncs to the Mac,
# run once in the escape_rooms repo:  git rm -r --cached . && git add . && git commit
# (re-applies these rules; disk files are untouched, git just stops tracking the ignored ones.)

# Design records + authoring docs (root/**/AGENTS.md already ignored above)
**/notes.md
**/wiring_checklist.md
# All backup / pre-edit snapshots (broadens the scenario.json.bak line above)
**/*.bak
**/scenario.json.pre_*
# Python build/test caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# ALL history-tier archive dirs (the z_ convention), not just z_history/
z_*/
**/z_*/

